1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,096
20 July 2026.

2
00:00:01,096 --> 00:00:03,964
A march moving towards Parliament.

3
00:00:03,964 --> 00:00:06,410
And in front of it, tear gas.

4
00:00:06,860 --> 00:00:12,188
Two days later, the Delhi High Court
issued notice to the Centre

5
00:00:12,188 --> 00:00:17,100
and Delhi Police, and ordered all
video evidence preserved.

6
00:00:17,550 --> 00:00:22,245
The police said there was
stone-pelting and vandalism, five

7
00:00:22,245 --> 00:00:26,940
FIRs were filed, and everything
was handled professionally.

8
00:00:27,390 --> 00:00:29,404
The case is in court.

9
00:00:29,404 --> 00:00:32,090
But this picture is not new.

10
00:00:32,540 --> 00:00:34,963
Olympic medal-winning wrestlers.

11
00:00:34,963 --> 00:00:37,235
Students reading in a library.

12
00:00:37,235 --> 00:00:38,825
Homes burnt in riots.

13
00:00:38,825 --> 00:00:41,930
A twenty-one-year-old farmer at a border.

14
00:00:42,380 --> 00:00:45,834
Every time, the same question.

15
00:00:45,834 --> 00:00:49,173
Who does the police work for?

16
00:00:49,173 --> 00:00:50,324
The law...

17
00:00:50,324 --> 00:00:51,360
or power?

18
00:00:52,810 --> 00:00:56,800
In this film, what is proven
we will call proven.

19
00:00:56,800 --> 00:00:59,894
What is alleged, we will call alleged.

20
00:00:59,894 --> 00:01:03,070
And in every story, the other side too.

21
00:01:03,520 --> 00:01:05,252
First, a basic point.

22
00:01:05,252 --> 00:01:08,220
On whose orders does the police act?

23
00:01:08,670 --> 00:01:11,969
Under the Constitution, police
is a state subject.

24
00:01:11,969 --> 00:01:14,871
So in most states, the
police sits under the

25
00:01:14,871 --> 00:01:17,840
Chief Minister and the
state Home Department.

26
00:01:18,290 --> 00:01:20,274
But Delhi is different.

27
00:01:20,274 --> 00:01:27,260
Delhi Police reports not to the Delhi
government, but to the Union Home Ministry.

28
00:01:27,710 --> 00:01:31,338
Since 2014 the BJP has
governed at the Centre, and

29
00:01:31,338 --> 00:01:34,530
since 2019 Amit Shah has
been Home Minister.

30
00:01:34,980 --> 00:01:39,237
So in every Delhi story in this
film, the last link of

31
00:01:39,237 --> 00:01:43,730
administrative responsibility is
the Union Home Ministry.

32
00:01:44,180 --> 00:01:49,819
But note: administrative
responsibility is not a direct order.

33
00:01:49,819 --> 00:01:54,640
We found no evidence that any
minister ordered force.

34
00:01:55,090 --> 00:01:59,778
The question is not about orders,
it is about accountability.

35
00:01:59,778 --> 00:02:01,930
So let's go to the evidence.

36
00:02:02,380 --> 00:02:03,293
January 2023.

37
00:02:03,293 --> 00:02:07,930
Some of India's biggest wrestlers sat
in protest at Jantar Mantar.

38
00:02:08,380 --> 00:02:12,982
The allegation: sexual harassment
of women wrestlers by the

39
00:02:12,982 --> 00:02:17,350
then federation chief, BJP MP
Brij Bhushan Sharan Singh.

40
00:02:17,800 --> 00:02:21,739
In April a written complaint
was given to the police.

41
00:02:21,739 --> 00:02:22,705
Still no FIR.

42
00:02:22,705 --> 00:02:26,347
The wrestlers went to the
Supreme Court, and only

43
00:02:26,347 --> 00:02:29,320
then, on 28 April, were FIRs registered.

44
00:02:29,770 --> 00:02:31,521
Then came 28 May 2023.

45
00:02:31,521 --> 00:02:34,624
The inauguration of the new Parliament.

46
00:02:34,624 --> 00:02:39,160
That same day, the wrestlers set
out to march towards it.

47
00:02:39,610 --> 00:02:41,956
There was pushing at the barricades.

48
00:02:41,956 --> 00:02:45,800
Olympic medallists were pulled
away and taken off in buses.

49
00:02:46,250 --> 00:02:51,150
That evening the Jantar Mantar
protest site was cleared.

50
00:02:51,600 --> 00:02:59,270
According to police, 700 people were
detained, and all were released by evening.

51
00:02:59,720 --> 00:03:04,621
And an FIR against the wrestlers,
including for rioting.

52
00:03:04,621 --> 00:03:07,859
Police claimed they broke barricades.

53
00:03:07,859 --> 00:03:09,960
Bajrang Punia denied it.

54
00:03:10,410 --> 00:03:14,643
So for an FIR against the
man accused of sexual

55
00:03:14,643 --> 00:03:18,967
harassment, they had to go to
the Supreme Court.

56
00:03:18,967 --> 00:03:23,200
Against the accusers, an FIR
came the same day.

57
00:03:24,450 --> 00:03:26,267
What happened in court?

58
00:03:26,267 --> 00:03:30,850
In May 2024 the court framed
charges against Brij Bhushan.

59
00:03:31,300 --> 00:03:35,064
The POCSO case involving the
minor wrestler was closed

60
00:03:35,064 --> 00:03:38,340
in May 2025, after the
complaint was withdrawn.

61
00:03:38,790 --> 00:03:42,840
And according to reports, on
3 August 2026 the

62
00:03:42,840 --> 00:03:46,890
court acquitted him in the
remaining case too.

63
00:03:47,340 --> 00:03:49,994
The court's verdict stands.

64
00:03:49,994 --> 00:03:56,090
But this film questions the police's
conduct, not the verdict.

65
00:03:56,540 --> 00:03:59,097
Come home with a medal, you get a salute.

66
00:03:59,097 --> 00:04:01,030
Ask for justice, you get a bus.

67
00:04:02,480 --> 00:04:03,733
15 December 2019.

68
00:04:03,733 --> 00:04:06,459
Protests against the citizenship law.

69
00:04:06,459 --> 00:04:08,670
Jamia Millia Islamia in Delhi.

70
00:04:09,120 --> 00:04:12,900
In the evening the protest turned
violent and buses were burnt.

71
00:04:12,900 --> 00:04:14,460
Police entered the campus.

72
00:04:14,910 --> 00:04:22,800
Police said they were chasing rioters,
and denied entering the library.

73
00:04:23,250 --> 00:04:28,590
Two months later, in February 2020,
the library CCTV came out.

74
00:04:29,040 --> 00:04:32,073
The footage appears to show
students sitting in

75
00:04:32,073 --> 00:04:34,590
the reading room being hit with batons.

76
00:04:35,040 --> 00:04:40,982
A police-linked video claimed
students were holding stones.

77
00:04:40,982 --> 00:04:47,830
A later fact-check found they were
barricading the door with tables.

78
00:04:48,280 --> 00:04:50,168
The NHRC report came.

79
00:04:50,168 --> 00:04:57,450
It called the caning in the library
avoidable, an irresponsible action by police.

80
00:04:57,900 --> 00:05:03,104
But the same report also said the
protest was unauthorised and

81
00:05:03,104 --> 00:05:08,140
violent, and that the real actors
behind it be investigated.

82
00:05:08,590 --> 00:05:11,332
The commission said the policemen who used

83
00:05:11,332 --> 00:05:14,140
batons in the library
should be identified.

84
00:05:14,590 --> 00:05:21,840
Nearly seven years on, we found no public
record of action against any policeman.

85
00:05:22,290 --> 00:05:26,765
And in October 2026 the Delhi High
Court dismissed petitions

86
00:05:26,765 --> 00:05:31,240
seeking an independent probe into
Jamia and the Delhi riots.

87
00:05:31,690 --> 00:05:32,738
February 2020.

88
00:05:32,738 --> 00:05:34,011
North-East Delhi.

89
00:05:34,011 --> 00:05:35,733
Three days of violence.

90
00:05:35,733 --> 00:05:37,680
Fifty-three people killed.

91
00:05:39,130 --> 00:05:41,105
Hundreds of cases were filed.

92
00:05:41,105 --> 00:05:43,830
The investigation was with Delhi Police.

93
00:05:44,280 --> 00:05:46,817
Now the court verdicts are arriving.

94
00:05:46,817 --> 00:05:51,750
And in many of them, the questions are
about the police investigation.

95
00:05:52,200 --> 00:05:56,156
The Indian Express read 93
acquittal orders.

96
00:05:56,156 --> 00:06:01,000
In 17, courts flagged fabricated
evidence or serious impropriety.

97
00:06:02,450 --> 00:06:08,384
In one case the court cited
"artificiality" in police claims.

98
00:06:08,384 --> 00:06:12,470
In another, it called an arson case false.

99
00:06:12,920 --> 00:06:17,932
In 2021 a Karkardooma Court judge wrote
that when history looks back at

100
00:06:17,932 --> 00:06:22,520
these riots, it will see the failure
of the investigating agency.

101
00:06:23,770 --> 00:06:30,390
In October 2021, in a routine High Court
reshuffle, he was transferred.

102
00:06:30,840 --> 00:06:35,340
Delhi Police says its
investigation was thorough, and

103
00:06:35,340 --> 00:06:39,160
there have been convictions
in several cases.

104
00:06:39,610 --> 00:06:44,423
And in October 2026 the High Court
said there was no material to

105
00:06:44,423 --> 00:06:48,560
show the investigation was
institutionally compromised.

106
00:06:49,010 --> 00:06:54,203
The figures before the
court: 22 convictions.

107
00:06:54,203 --> 00:06:55,934
108 acquittals.

108
00:06:55,934 --> 00:06:57,550
16 discharges.

109
00:06:57,000 --> 00:07:01,909
So the court did not find a
conspiracy in the probe.

110
00:07:01,909 --> 00:07:07,170
But those acquitted spent years on
trial, and many spent time in jail.

111
00:07:07,620 --> 00:07:08,911
The same question.

112
00:07:08,911 --> 00:07:12,497
When a court itself calls
evidence fabricated, who

113
00:07:12,497 --> 00:07:15,510
acts against the person who fabricated it?

114
00:07:16,960 --> 00:07:18,063
February 2024.

115
00:07:18,063 --> 00:07:23,580
Farmers set out for Delhi, demanding a
legal guarantee on crop prices.

116
00:07:24,030 --> 00:07:27,765
Haryana's BJP government
sealed the road at

117
00:07:27,765 --> 00:07:31,500
Shambhu and Khanauri, on
the Punjab border.

118
00:07:31,950 --> 00:07:35,686
Tear-gas shells were dropped from drones.

119
00:07:35,686 --> 00:07:43,250
According to Amnesty, police sources
themselves spoke of 4,500 shells in six hours.

120
00:07:43,700 --> 00:07:49,890
Police said protesters threw stones and
several personnel were injured.

121
00:07:50,340 --> 00:07:51,196
21 February.

122
00:07:51,196 --> 00:07:51,837
Khanauri.

123
00:07:51,837 --> 00:07:55,260
Twenty-one-year-old
Shubhkaran Singh was killed.

124
00:07:57,210 --> 00:07:58,597
Whose shot was it?

125
00:07:58,597 --> 00:08:01,524
Haryana did not accept responsibility.

126
00:08:01,524 --> 00:08:05,530
And in Punjab, even the FIR
came about a week later.

127
00:08:05,980 --> 00:08:10,212
Then the Punjab and Haryana
High Court said both

128
00:08:10,212 --> 00:08:13,650
states have several things to cover up.

129
00:08:14,100 --> 00:08:19,272
The court set up an inquiry panel
led by a retired judge.

130
00:08:19,272 --> 00:08:22,630
The Supreme Court refused to stay it.

131
00:08:23,080 --> 00:08:29,270
Nearly three years on, we found
no public final report.

132
00:08:29,720 --> 00:08:30,692
One border.

133
00:08:30,692 --> 00:08:32,107
Two governments.

134
00:08:32,107 --> 00:08:34,052
Two different parties.

135
00:08:34,052 --> 00:08:36,350
And no answer from either.

136
00:08:37,800 --> 00:08:40,457
Now let's go inside the police station.

137
00:08:40,457 --> 00:08:42,500
Where there are fewer cameras.

138
00:08:42,950 --> 00:08:44,215
NHRC figures.

139
00:08:44,215 --> 00:08:48,887
Deaths in police custody: 176
in 2021-22, 163 in

140
00:08:48,887 --> 00:08:52,780
2022-23, 157 in 2023-24, 140 in 2024-25.

141
00:08:53,230 --> 00:08:54,831
The number has fallen.

142
00:08:54,831 --> 00:09:00,070
But every year, on average, one death in
police custody every third day.

143
00:09:00,520 --> 00:09:02,897
Not every death is a crime.

144
00:09:02,897 --> 00:09:04,834
Some are from illness.

145
00:09:04,834 --> 00:09:09,060
But to know the truth, there
must be an inquiry.

146
00:09:09,510 --> 00:09:10,828
And convictions?

147
00:09:10,828 --> 00:09:16,098
According to reports based on NCRB
data, for several years after

148
00:09:16,098 --> 00:09:21,450
2018, not a single policeman was
convicted for a custodial death.

149
00:09:22,700 --> 00:09:26,320
This is not the story of only one party.

150
00:09:26,770 --> 00:09:29,396
Uttar Pradesh, BJP government.

151
00:09:29,396 --> 00:09:33,423
By the police's own figures,
from 2017 to July

152
00:09:33,423 --> 00:09:37,450
2025: nearly 15,000
encounters and 238 deaths.

153
00:09:37,900 --> 00:09:43,002
The government says this was return
fire against armed criminals.

154
00:09:43,002 --> 00:09:46,220
Critics call it punishment without trial.

155
00:09:46,670 --> 00:09:49,024
Telangana, then under the TRS.

156
00:09:49,024 --> 00:09:54,360
In 2019, four men accused of rape were
killed in a police encounter.

157
00:09:54,810 --> 00:09:58,645
A commission set up by the
Supreme Court called it

158
00:09:58,645 --> 00:10:02,480
fake, and recommended that ten
policemen be tried.

159
00:10:02,930 --> 00:10:05,340
Tamil Nadu, 2020, under the AIADMK.

160
00:10:05,340 --> 00:10:08,231
A father and son, Jayaraj and Bennix, died

161
00:10:08,231 --> 00:10:11,260
after custody at
Sathankulam police station.

162
00:10:11,710 --> 00:10:13,693
The CBI investigated.

163
00:10:13,693 --> 00:10:20,680
And in 2026, a court convicted nine
policemen and sentenced them to death.

164
00:10:21,130 --> 00:10:27,536
And in 2025, under the DMK government, Ajith
Kumar died in custody in Sivaganga.

165
00:10:27,536 --> 00:10:32,020
The Chief Minister apologised;
the case went to the CBI.

166
00:10:32,470 --> 00:10:33,996
BJP or opposition.

167
00:10:33,996 --> 00:10:38,660
Whoever controls the police is
the one who must answer.

168
00:10:39,110 --> 00:10:43,946
The only difference: Sathankulam
reached a conviction because the

169
00:10:43,946 --> 00:10:48,930
probe went to an outside agency and
the court kept up the pressure.

170
00:10:49,380 --> 00:10:51,484
So accountability is possible.

171
00:10:51,484 --> 00:10:54,080
The system just doesn't make it easy.

172
00:10:55,330 --> 00:11:00,230
And the Supreme Court said
this twenty years ago.

173
00:11:00,680 --> 00:11:02,715
2006, the Prakash Singh case.

174
00:11:02,715 --> 00:11:05,170
Seven directions for police reform.

175
00:11:05,620 --> 00:11:09,538
A security commission to shield
police from political pressure.

176
00:11:09,538 --> 00:11:11,217
A fixed tenure for the DGP.

177
00:11:11,217 --> 00:11:13,891
Investigation separated
from law and order.

178
00:11:13,891 --> 00:11:17,560
And an independent authority for
complaints against police.

179
00:11:18,010 --> 00:11:22,705
Fifteen years later, in
2021, a report found

180
00:11:22,705 --> 00:11:27,400
that not a single state was
fully complying.

181
00:11:27,850 --> 00:11:29,257
BJP states too.

182
00:11:29,257 --> 00:11:31,320
Opposition states too.

183
00:11:31,320 --> 00:11:35,540
No one likes giving up
control of the police.

184
00:11:35,990 --> 00:11:40,040
Your rights are written
clearly in the law.

185
00:11:40,490 --> 00:11:41,432
Article 19.

186
00:11:41,432 --> 00:11:45,630
The right to assemble
peaceably and without arms.

187
00:11:46,080 --> 00:11:46,993
Article 21.

188
00:11:46,993 --> 00:11:50,230
The right to life and personal liberty.

189
00:11:50,230 --> 00:11:53,550
It does not end inside a police station.

190
00:11:54,000 --> 00:11:54,813
Article 22.

191
00:11:54,813 --> 00:11:59,323
The right to know the grounds of
arrest, to consult a lawyer,

192
00:11:59,323 --> 00:12:03,390
and to be produced before a
magistrate within 24 hours.

193
00:12:03,840 --> 00:12:05,071
And the 1996 D.K.

194
00:12:05,071 --> 00:12:06,085
Basu judgment.

195
00:12:06,085 --> 00:12:11,950
An arrest memo for every arrest, informing
the family, and a medical examination.

196
00:12:12,400 --> 00:12:17,935
The police were given the
lathi to protect the law.

197
00:12:17,935 --> 00:12:19,020
Not power.

198
00:12:20,470 --> 00:12:25,182
Because the day the uniform
starts fearing those who ask

199
00:12:25,182 --> 00:12:29,220
questions, the Constitution
becomes just a book.

200
00:12:31,170 --> 00:12:34,094
Is the police accountable in your city?

201
00:12:34,094 --> 00:12:36,942
Share your experience in the comments.

202
00:12:36,942 --> 00:12:40,990
And if you want truth with
evidence, join the channel.
